# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the Windows machines this config is edited on,
# which checks files out with CRLF. `.stylua.toml` sets `line_endings = "Unix"`,
# so stylua then reports every Lua file as needing reformatting even when its
# content is already correct -- a whole-file diff where every line is both
# removed and added. That has twice sent a formatting run chasing a difference
# that was only line endings.
#
# This config is also used on macOS and Linux, where CRLF is simply wrong, and
# `claude/hooks/session-start.lua` and `claude/server.lua` are read by
# `nvim -l`, which is fussier about them than the editor is.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
